_model: proposition
---
title: Proposition 7
---
order: 7
---
short_label: IV.7
---
statement: To circumscribe a square about a given circle.
---
proof:

Let *ABCD* be the given circle.

It is required to circumscribe a square about the circle *ABCD.*

Draw two diameters *AC* and *BD* of the circle *ABCD* at right angles to one another. [!just III.1, I.11]

<div class="just"><a href="/elements/books/bookIII/propositions/propIII16/#cor">III.16,Cor</a></div>
Draw *FG, GH, HK,* and *KF* through the points *A, B, C,* and *D* touching the circle *ABCD.*

<figure class="diagram">
<canvas id="canvas_0" width="290" height="290" tabindex="0"></canvas>
<noscript><img alt="IV.7 diagram" src="propIV7.gif"/></noscript>
<script type="text/javascript">
    geomlib.init({
        canvasid: "canvas_0",
        background: "35,19,100",
        title: "IV.7",
        pivot: "E",
        elements: [
            "A;point;free;145,40",
            "C;point;free;145,250",
            "E;point;midpoint;A,C;black;green",
            "B;point;perpendicular;E,A",
            "D;point;perpendicular;E,C",
            "F;point;parallelogram;A,E,D",
            "G;point;parallelogram;B,E,A",
            "H;point;parallelogram;C,E,B",
            "K;point;parallelogram;D,E,C",
            "square;polygon;quadrilateral;F,G,H,K;0;0;black;random",
            "ABCD;circle;radius;E,A;0;0;black;random",
            "AC;line;connect;A,C",
            "BD;line;connect;B,D"
        ],
    });
</script>
</figure>

Then, since *FG* touches the circle *ABCD,* and *EA* has been joined from the center *E* to the point of contact at *A,* therefore the angles at A are right. For the same reason the angles at the points *B, C,* and *D* are also right. [!just III.18]

Now, since the angle *AEB* is right, and the angle *EBG* is also right, therefore *GH* is parallel to *AC.* [!just I.28]

For the same reason *AC* is also parallel to *FK,* so that *GH* is also parallel to *FK.* [!just I.30]

Similarly we can prove that each of the straight lines *GF* and *HK* is parallel to *BED.*

Therefore *GK, GC, AK, FB,* and *BK* are parallelograms, therefore *GF* equals *HK,* and *GH* equals *FK.* [!just I.34]

And, since *AC* equals *BD,* and *AC* also equals each of the straight lines *GH* and *FK,* and *BD* equals each of the straight lines *GF* and *HK,* therefore the quadrilateral *FGHK* is equilateral. [!just I.34]

I say next that it is also right-angled.

For, since *GBEA* is a parallelogram, and the angle *AEB* is right, therefore the angle *AGB* is also right. [!just I.34]

Similarly we can prove that the angles at *H, K,* and *F* are also right. Therefore *FGHK* is right-angled.

But it was also proved equilateral, therefore it is a square, and it has been circumscribed about the circle *ABCD.*

Therefore a square has been circumscribed about the given circle.

<div class="qed">Q.E.F.</div>
---
body:

This proposition is used in @XII.10.
